            <ArticleTitle>Laparoscopic Wedge Resection of Gastric Stromal Tumor (GIST).</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>203-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.5455/medarh.2015.69.203-205</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="INTRODUCTION" NlmCategory="BACKGROUND">Laparoscopic treatment in general, in recent age has proven that it is well associated with low morbidity, mortality, fast recovery, less pain and sound oncologic outcomes. Recent reports from the National Comprehensive Cancer Network (NCCN) GIST Task Force and the GIST Consensus Conference under the auspices of The European Society for Medical Oncology (ESMO) show that laparoscopic resection may be used for small gastric GISTs (&lt; 2 cm in size).</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CASE REPORT" NlmCategory="METHODS">We report, all the benefits of laparoscopic approach which include short hospitalization, less pain, better cosmetic effect and good oncological outcome, in this case report of 60 year old female patient with gastric GIST larger than 2 cm.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
